SUMMARY:Reflecting on Resilience - Exhibit Opening
DESCRIPTION:For 75 years\, stewardship in the TSF has taken many forms – from the daily labor of rebuilding a burned landscape to welcoming visitors into a living classroom. Reflecting on Resilience explores the intertwined histories of service\, restoration\, and public engagement that connect South Fork Forest Camp and the Tillamook Forest Center. Through stories\, artifacts\, and never before publicly displayed photos\, this exhibit invites reflection on how forests\, and our relationship to them\, change over time\, and how today’s stewardship will define the forests of the future. \nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/reflecting-on-resilience-exhibit-opening/
LOCATION:Tillamook Forest Center\, 45500 Wilson River Highway\, Tillamook\, OR\, 97141\, United States
CATEGORIES:Educational,Kids Calendar,Plants & Nature
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/Film-Strip-website-small-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Tillamook Forest Center":MAILTO:Alejandra.Arellano@odf.oregon.gov
END:VEVENT
