SUMMARY:Spring Break: Bugs & Beaks
DESCRIPTION:Spread your wings and go wild this Spring Break at the Hands On Children’s Museum! Enjoy feathered fun with live animals\, bird and bug science\, and hands-on flying crafts. \nLive Animal Guests & Special Experiences: \n• Meet live raptors with The Falconer and visit friendly chickens from Animal Encounters Petting Zoo.\n• Get up close with insects from Pest Stop and learn which bugs are helpful (and even edible!).\n• Discover how birds evolved from dinosaurs with experts from the Burke Museum.\n• Learn backyard birding tips with the South Sound Bird Alliance and build a feeder in our MakeSpace.\n• Enjoy high-energy science demos with Dr. Science and music and stories at Rock N’ Read with Liza. \nPresented by: Watson’s Greenhouse\nThe Falconer Sponsored by: Wild Birds Unlimited\nCreepy Crawlies & Crickets Sponsored by: Pest Stop
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/spring-break-bugs-beaks/2026-04-01/
LOCATION:Hands On Children’s Museum\, 414 Jefferson St. NE\, Olympia\, WA\, 98501\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts/Crafts,Educational,Family Fun,Indoor,Indoor Play Park,Kids Calendar,Museum,Outdoor,STEM
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/Birds2.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Hands On Children's Museum":MAILTO:info@hocm.org
GEO:47.0480478;-122.8965656
